From 8fab837aef6a8f12d8590df5fbde5fed39de156d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:17:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] libc: read system properties from a file

Replace the __system_property_get/find/read stubs with a small
in-memory property table loaded from a text file, one name=value per
line, named by BIONIC_PROPS_FILE or <BIONIC_VENDOR_ROOT>/t2-props.
Libraries that configure themselves from properties (ro.hardware.*,
ro.vendor.*, debug.*, persist.*) can then be given exactly the values
they expect.

Added on top of the old API: __system_property_read_callback,
__system_property_foreach, __system_property_set (in-memory only),
__system_property_serial and __system_property_area_serial.

When no file is configured the old behaviour is kept, so existing
users see no change: ro.build.version.sdk reads as 21 and every other
property is empty. __system_property_find no longer leaks one
allocation per call; prop_info pointers point into a table that only
grows, as callers expect them to stay valid.
